  "planning_notes": [
    "All required wired pins were represented: D2, D3 (two near sensors), D8/D9 (HC-SR04 trig/echo), D4/D5 (TM1637), D6 (buzzer tone), D13 (LED), D7 (reset button). No other GPIO/RGB operations were explicitly wired in the provided facts; therefore no additional ports were created.",
    "TM1637 output is modeled as a single tm1637_number showing the aggregated total count; the two-category counting, stopping logic, and reset behavior are SysML responsibilities.",
    "Ultrasonic sample_period_ms was not specified; model should choose a control-period-multiple >= ceil((timeout_us+12)/1000) and >=60ms, with timeout_us set to 30000us (within 25000..60000).",
    "Serial protocol for the required 'empty bin needed' message was not fixed as an exact fixed text line in the prompt. Therefore, serial reporting is assumed to be typed numeric status/state + last fill height in one trigger group, and any exact code mapping must be defined in SysML.",
    "Near sensors on D2/D3 are assumed to produce digital HIGH when an object is present; pullup enabled and initial=false. If the actual sensors are active-low, this must be corrected in SysML modeling (not by inverting ports here, per requirements).",
    "Reset button on D7 is assumed active-high when pressed with pullup enabled; initial=false."
  ],
